FEATURE: list-scroller-verification
DATE: 2026-10-05
SCOPE: verify the ListScroller module, fix what is broken, and document it

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The vUX library (this repository). The workspace consumers (Apps/vGet and
Apps/myinvitees/app.myinvitees.com) mount vUX through a symlink and pick up changes on the next page
load. Neither imports vUX-listScroller.js directly; any page using the FormComponents datePicker
with a range over 11 decades uses it through the picker, whose behaviour was re-verified.

Consumer-visible surface:
  - vUX-listScroller.js          internals rebuilt; public API unchanged. Presses measured from the
                                 real position, scrollSpeed and paddingRight now work, config is
                                 live, stricter validation, buttons start inactive at initialize().
  - assets/css/listScroller.css  list in normal flow (no absolute positioning), container width no
                                 longer forced, late-added items covered.
  - vUX-formComponents.js        one ListScroller per date picker instead of per builder;
                                 datePicker destroy() destroys them all.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION METHOD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No test runner exists. Headless Chromium (chrome-headless-shell) was driven in real time over the
DevTools protocol (virtual-time mode runs only one requestAnimationFrame, so it cannot test the
scroll animation), against pages served with python3 -m http.server. The same suite ran against
the original files.

Baseline (original code):   21 passed, 27 failed
After the fixes:            48 passed, 0 failed
Example page suite:         15 passed, 0 failed  (at 1280px and at 375px), plus visual review of
                            full-page screenshots at both widths
datePicker (1700-2030 range, two decade boxes): Next/Prev and button states correct; Prev from the
                            end now moves, which it did not before

The harnesses live in the session scratchpad, not the repository. Not verified: real touch devices,
or browsers other than Chromium.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFECTS FOUND AND FIXED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 1. $$.animate() kept its own start value; at the row's end it overshot with no scroll event to
    correct it, so the next opposite press moved nothing. Two quick presses moved 317px, not 450.
 2. The list width was item count x scrollSize, so the row scrolled into empty space.
 3. The list was position:absolute, collapsing the container to 0px height.
 4. Button state never updated on a container-only resize, new items, or the stylesheet arriving.
 5. Clicks on an icon inside a button were ignored (delegated handler checked e.target only).
 6. A manual scroll after offScroller() re-enabled both buttons.
 7. offScroller() threw a TypeError with hasButtons = false.
 8. wrapperStyle replaced the container's whole inline style; the stylesheet's width:100%!important
    made a wrapperStyle width ineffective.
 9. scrollSpeed and paddingRight were stored and never used.
10. destroy() left container scroll classes, wrapperStyle, button classes and cursor behind.
11. Accepted at assignment, failing later: list outside container, same button twice,
    scrollSize <= 0 / NaN, negative scrollSpeed, class name with spaces.
12. scrollSpeed's error said "must be an array"; the dead 'children < 0' check is removed.
13. datePicker destroy() did not release its ListScroller.
14. (follow-up) The datePicker shared one ListScroller per builder, so only the first picker opened
    got working decade arrows, and a later picker's decade pick or Back drove the first one's.
    Each picker now has its own scroller; destroy() releases them all. Verified with two
    long-range pickers on one builder.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KNOWN LIMITATIONS (documented, not changed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 - Horizontal only, and no events; consumers watch the buttons' class or the container's scroll.
 - config properties are write-only, as across vUX.
 - The default wrapperStyle width:100% is inline and outranks a stylesheet width.
